      {
        "id": "common-affected-engines-and-root-causes",
        "title": "Common affected engines and root causes",
        "description": "According to UK independent specialist consensus:",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Rod knock is most common in high-mileage vehicles (80,000+ miles) with irregular oil changes.",
              "Oil pump failure causes rod knock: VAG 1.8T/2.0T and BMW N20 engines are known for oil pump issues.",
              "Low oil levels are a primary cause: 60% of rod knock cases occur in vehicles that were 1+ litres low on oil.",
              "Any engine can suffer rod knock - proper oil maintenance is your only defence."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h3",
            "id": "",
            "text": "BMW N47/N57 diesel"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "High incidence of rod knock linked to oil pump drive chain failures and irregular oil changes."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "£1,000-£1,800"
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": "h3",
            "id": "",
            "text": "Subaru EJ series"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Notorious for rod bearing failure, especially in turbocharged variants. Oil starvation is a primary cause."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
